Subject: [PATCH] dns integration: register a class TLD before creating zones

Designate validates a zone name against the TLD list only while that list is
non-empty, and the list is deployment global. An empty list disables the TLD
restriction alone -- _is_valid_zone_name still enforces max_zone_name_len,
the more-than-one-label rule and the blacklist unconditionally. Once a TLD
exists the name must additionally carry a registered TLD as one of its own
suffixes: central/service.py walks every trailing label sequence, from the
whole name down to the last label, and raises InvalidZoneName('Invalid TLD')
only when none of them matches.

designate-tempest-plugin's BaseZonesTest.resource_setup registers a
class-scoped TLD and generates its own zones beneath it, so it is correct for
itself regardless of the switch. But the TLD stays live for the whole class,
which flips the deployment into enforcing mode for everybody else running at
the same time.

neutron-tempest-plugin's scenario/test_dns_integration.py does neither. All
four classes create zones: three inherit BaseDNSIntegrationTests.resource_setup,
which calls rand_zone_name() and so lands under designate's default
[dns] tld_suffix, and DNSIntegrationDomainPerProjectTests hardcodes a ".zone."
suffix. None registers a TLD, so all four depend on what else is running:
concurrent tests can register TLDs that do not match neutron's generated zone
names, and then every create_zone in this module fails.

Under OSISM's all-plugin tempest discovery designate's zone tests and neutron's
DNS tests run concurrently against one deployment, and the classes collide:

    setUpClass (neutron_tempest_plugin.scenario.test_dns_integration.
                DNSIntegrationTests)
    setUpClass (neutron_tempest_plugin.scenario.test_dns_integration.
                DNSIntegrationExtraTests)

    tempest.lib.exceptions.BadRequest: Bad request
    Details: {'code': 400, 'type': 'invalid_zone_name',
              'message': 'Invalid TLD'}

Both died in resource_setup on create_zone. Reconstructing the TLD balance from
the controllers' designate access logs (successful POST/DELETE /v2/tlds only)
showed exactly one TLD live at each failure moment, inside windows of 2-4
minutes separated by gaps at zero -- a race whose outcome depends on whether a
zone class happens to be running.

Fix it on the victim side, the same way designate-tempest-plugin fixed itself in
ade263c ("Fix TLD issues for test concurrency", 2022-05-23): give each class a
private TLD and generate its zones beneath it. _setup_class_tld() registers a
unique TLD with the admin client and is called from both resource_setup paths --
the base one, plus DNSIntegrationDomainPerProjectTests, which deliberately skips
the base setup. That class keeps its "<user_id>.<project_id>" domain template;
only the dead ".zone." suffix is replaced by the registered TLD.

The TLD cleanup is registered before the zones that live under it. Class
resource cleanups run in reverse order of registration, so the zones are deleted
first and the TLD outlives its dependants.

Registering a TLD costs nothing and needs no lock, unlike marking designate's
zone classes @serial, which would block every other test for the lifetime of
each class.

Self-expiring: this patch is applied by the tempest image build with
`patch --forward --dry-run` gating. Once neutron-tempest-plugin ships this
upstream the patch will no longer apply, the build will fail, and this file must
be deleted.

--- a/neutron_tempest_plugin/scenario/test_dns_integration.py
+++ b/neutron_tempest_plugin/scenario/test_dns_integration.py
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@
         super().setup_clients()
         cls.zone_client = cls.os_tempest.dns_v2.ZonesClient()
         cls.recordset_client = cls.os_tempest.dns_v2.RecordsetClient()
+        cls.admin_tld_client = cls.os_admin.dns_v2.TldClient()
         cls.query_client.build_timeout = 60
 
     @classmethod
@@ -78,11 +79,42 @@
             raise cls.skipException("Designate tempest plugin is missing")
 
     @classmethod
+    def _setup_class_tld(cls):
+        """Register a private, class scoped TLD and export it as cls.tld_name.
+
+        Designate checks a zone name against the TLD list only while that
+        list is non-empty, and the list is deployment global.  An empty list
+        disables the TLD restriction alone -- length, label count and the
+        blacklist are still enforced.  While the list is non-empty the name
+        must additionally carry one of its own suffixes as a registered TLD.
+
+        Concurrent tests can register TLDs that do not match the zone names
+        generated here -- designate-tempest-plugin's zone classes each
+        register a class scoped TLD -- and then every zone this module
+        creates comes back as a 400 "Invalid TLD".  Generating our zones
+        beneath a TLD we register ourselves makes the suffix match by
+        construction, independently of what else runs against the same
+        deployment: the fix designate-tempest-plugin made for itself in
+        ade263c ("Fix TLD issues for test concurrency").
+        """
+        tld_name = dns_data_utils.rand_zone_name(name="dnsintegration")
+        cls.tld_name = ".{}".format(tld_name)
+        cls.class_tld = cls.admin_tld_client.create_tld(
+            tld_name=tld_name[:-1])
+        # Registered before any zone underneath it: class resource cleanups
+        # run in reverse order of registration, so the TLD is removed only
+        # after the zones that depend on it.
+        cls.addClassResourceCleanup(
+            cls.admin_tld_client.delete_tld, cls.class_tld[1]['id'],
+            ignore_errors=lib_exc.NotFound)
+
+    @classmethod
     @utils.requires_ext(extension="dns-integration", service="network")
     def resource_setup(cls):
         super().resource_setup()
+        cls._setup_class_tld()
         cls.zone_name = dns_data_utils.rand_zone_name(
-            name="basednsintegrationtests")
+            name="basednsintegrationtests", suffix=cls.tld_name)
         cls.zone = cls.zone_client.create_zone(
             name=cls.zone_name, wait_until='ACTIVE')[1]
         cls.addClassResourceCleanup(
@@ -311,11 +343,13 @@
     @classmethod
     def resource_setup(cls):
         super(BaseDNSIntegrationTests, cls).resource_setup()
+        cls._setup_class_tld()
         cls.name = data_utils.rand_name('test-domain')
-        cls.zone_name = "%s.%s.%s.zone." % (cls.client.user_id,
-                                        cls.client.project_id,
-                                        cls.name)
-        dns_domain_template = "<user_id>.<project_id>.%s.zone." % cls.name
+        cls.zone_name = "%s.%s.%s%s" % (
+            cls.client.user_id, cls.client.project_id, cls.name,
+            cls.tld_name)
+        dns_domain_template = "<user_id>.<project_id>.%s%s" % (
+            cls.name, cls.tld_name)
         cls.zone = cls.zone_client.create_zone(
             name=cls.zone_name, wait_until='ACTIVE')[1]
         cls.addClassResourceCleanup(cls.zone_client.delete_zone,
